   syntax: #import <filename>
   Where filename is something like testme.  Don't include the py
   extension, though.
   This will import/reload the module <filename>.
   You can build your own commands this way.  Example:
   ---------------------myfile.py--------------------
   from exported import *
   import myfile

   def mycommand(words, input, seslist):
      lyntin_command('#showme hey dude--this is my function!')

      lyntin_command('say I have this sudden urge to kill ' + words[1])



   # lyntin_add_command is from the exported module.
   lyntin_add_command("mykill", myfile.mycommand)
   --------------------------------------------------
